<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>1.3.1: Finding a Relationship between 𝒙 and 𝒚</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m00091</md:content-id>
    <md:title>1.3.1: Finding a Relationship between 𝒙 and 𝒚</md:title>
    <md:uuid>4c75e607-3daf-4dd5-8149-39bf47140801</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
    <section class="numbered-exercises" id="sect-00001"><title>Warm Up</title>
      <para id="para-00001">Here is a table of values. The two quantities, <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> and <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>, are related.</para>
      <table class="unnumbered os-raise-skinnytable unnumbered" id="table-00001">
        <tgroup cols="2">
        
  <tbody>
            <row>
              <entry><m:math><m:mrow><m:mn>1</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></entry>
              <entry><m:math><m:mrow><m:mn>0</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></entry>
            </row>
            <row>
              <entry><m:math><m:mrow><m:mn>3</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></entry>
              <entry><m:math><m:mrow><m:mn>8</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></entry>
            </row>
            <row>
              <entry><m:math><m:mrow><m:mn>5</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></entry>
              <entry><m:math><m:mrow><m:mn>24</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></entry>
            </row>
            <row>
              <entry><m:math><m:mrow><m:mn>7</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></entry>
              <entry><m:math><m:mrow><m:mn>48</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math></entry>
            </row>
          </tbody>
        </tgroup>
      </table>
      <exercise id="exer-00001">
        <problem id="prob-00001">
          <para id="para-00002">What are some strategies you could use to find a relationship between <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> and <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>? Brainstorm as many ways as possible.</para>
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00001">
          <para id="para-00003">Your answer may vary, but here are some samples:</para>
          <list id="list-00001">
            <item>See if there is an operation that could be done to <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> that would produce <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>.</item>
            <item>Compare how the <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>-values change and the <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>-values change, and see if there is a pattern.</item>
            <item>See if the numbers in one column follow a special pattern and if that pattern could be connected to the numbers in the other column.</item>
            <item>Plot the <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>- and <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>-values on a coordinate plane and see if the graph looks like a familiar relationship.</item>
          </list>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
    </section>
  </content>
</document>
